# Bigint remainder keeps the dividend sign

Takes a 31-digit value and its negation modulo 7 to verify the remainder
keeps the dividend sign in both cases, producing 1 and -1.

>>> source
dividend: bigint = 1000000000000000000000000000000
neg_dividend: bigint = -1000000000000000000000000000000
divisor: bigint = 7

// Verifies the remainder of a positive dividend.
positive_remainder: bigint = dividend % divisor
print(positive_remainder)

// Verifies the remainder takes the dividend sign for a negative dividend.
neg_remainder: bigint = neg_dividend % divisor
print(neg_remainder)

<<< stdout
1
-1

<<< stderr
